From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:25:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08091/11362] Generation-validity is no longer the binding
 constraint; inertness is the largest class

Classified all 412 frozen induced-engine candidates on disk with the SHIPPED
detector (arc_engine_static_validation.validate_engine_code), stratified by
generator and by retry regime.

The premise this was set from does not hold on the shipped path. "22 of 40
unusable" is a SINGLE-SHOT figure: with retry off 45.8% of best-of-N candidates
are guaranteed downstream rejects, but under the shipped 3-try induce loop the
same generator leaves 8.9% mechanically unusable and 21.0% guaranteed-reject.

Across 172 gemma-4-31B candidates: clean-and-live 124 (72.1%), INERT 26 (15.1%),
no code after all tries 8 (4.7%), syntax error 7 (4.1%), engine raises 3 (1.7%),
one each of truncated / non-terminating / goal-raises. Inertness is the largest
failure class and exceeds every code-validity class combined, under either
precedence assignment.

Recommended: wire the already-shipped engine_changes_anything into
_engine_defects, reusing the existing one-reask budget. Provably safe (0 of 11
inert candidates were plannable) and worth +0.75 PLANNABLE candidates per 100
generations, with a multiplier CI including zero. That small number is the
finding: 49 of 124 cells score exactly 0.0 held-out change fidelity and only 15
of them are mechanically visible -- the other 34 are live engines predicting the
wrong cells, which no static check, grammar or repair loop can see.

MANDATORY precondition, measured not assumed: engine_changes_anything is NOT
bounded. The 2026-08-01 hardening put dry_run_defects behind a killable
subprocess and left this sibling in-process. Measured on ft09_k5: the bounded
call returns in 30.07s with engine_nonterminating; the unbounded sibling does
not return. Wiring it as-is reintroduces the 2026-07-31 13-minute hang.

Reproduction: extracted-code sha reproduces on 48/48 best-of-N candidates and
defect kinds on 47/47 scorable ones. A bug this pass made and caught is recorded
in the artifact -- the first version fed best-of-N a rebuilt A/B window instead
of its own captured prefix, producing 10 spurious "inert" verdicts including on
ft09_k1, one of only two plannable candidates in the corpus.

adversarial_verify: 5 artifacts scanned, 0 flagged.

